Subject: [PATCH] Recompiler: the parallel halfword multiplies (PMULTH, PMADDH, PMSUBH, PHMADH, PHMSBH) and PMFHL.LH by lane

The five translated as one dot product: all eight 16x16 products summed into a single 64-bit value written to LO/HI
and rd. On the EE each product has its own 32-bit word: PMULTH / PMADDH / PMSUBH set, add to or take from LO.w0 p0,
LO.w1 p1, HI.w0 p2, HI.w1 p3, LO.w2 p4, LO.w3 p5, HI.w2 p6, HI.w3 p7; PHMADH / PHMSBH put the pairs' sum (difference)
in LO.w0, HI.w0, LO.w2, HI.w2 and the odd product (its complement) beside it, as PCSX2 has them; rd = LO.w0, HI.w0,
LO.w2, HI.w2. LO's and HI's upper 64 bits are ctx->lo1 / ctx->hi1 (the MULT1 pipeline's registers, which are
LO/HI's upper halves on the EE). PMFHL.LH read only the lower halves and saturated: now the low halfword of each of
the eight words, truncated.

For Transformers: three colour blends - the CPU particle managers' gradient (0x3711A0: the Antarctica plane's smoke
had alpha 0 on every particle), 0x407270 and 0x555E30 - each (a * (128 - w) + b * w) >> 7 per byte with PMULTH,
PMADDH, PMFHL.LH.

ps2xRecomp:
- mmi_translation_helpers.cpp: halfwordMultiply (the five), PMFHL.LH by lane.

diff --git a/ps2xRecomp/src/lib/mmi_translation_helpers.cpp b/ps2xRecomp/src/lib/mmi_translation_helpers.cpp
index a2bcb77..c925589 100644
--- a/ps2xRecomp/src/lib/mmi_translation_helpers.cpp
